BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sunnycoast-rke8y@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260926T140000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260926T160000
SUMMARY:Inspector Drake & The Black Widow by BATS
DESCRIPTION:BATS THEATRE COMPANY PROUDLY PRESENTS - INSPECTOR DRAKE AND THE
  BLACK WIDOW Imagine if Fawlty Towers meets a murder mystery. That is\, es
 sentially\, Inspector Drake and the Black Widow. A classic English farce f
 eaturing a cross between ‘Inspector Clouseau’ and ‘And Then There We
 re None’ will have you laughing out loud and forgetting about the outsid
 e world. A dead body is found\, whilst dusting at 3am\, which sets up a pl
 ay that is an amusing parody of the whodunnit genre\, that’s packed with
  lots of visual gags\, subtle adult innuendo\, all topped with a touch of 
 cross-dressing. The plot\, set in the 1920s \, has Sergeant Plod send for 
 the infamous Inspector Drake to help solve the murder of John Johnson who 
 has been stabbed in the back whilst wearing his wife’s dress. The two ar
 e thwarted by a series of women who look suspiciously alike\, with triplet
 s born two months apart\, a missing semi-tropical spider and a lustful wid
 ow. Just a few of the obstacles facing Inspector Drake. Imagine Basil Fawl
 ty playing Inspector Clouseau playing Inspector Drake? What can possibly g
 o wrong? From the Team at BATS Theatre\, that brought you ‘Sex Please\, 
 We’re Sixty’. PERFORMANCE DATES: Friday\, 25 September 2026 at 7.30pm 
 Saturday\, 26 September 2026 at 2.00pm and 7.30pm Friday\, 2 October 2026 
 at 7.30pm Saturday\, 3 October 2026 at 2.00pm and 7.30pm
LOCATION:Buderim War Memorial Community Association\, 50 Burnett Street
URL:https://www.bwmca.com.au/events-2-1/inspector-drake-the-black-widow-by-
 bats-k9h22
END:VEVENT
